`serde_json::Value` enables arbitrary field renames, additions, removals, and transforms independent of current Rust struct shape; (3) version bounds checking rejects both future (SchemaVersionTooNew) and too-old (SchemaVersionTooOld) saves with clear errors; (4) the real v2→v3 migration (net-volume rescaling) has thorough error handling for malformed legacy geometry/substrate data; (5) the v3→v4 no-op migration correctly relies on `#[serde(default)]` while maintaining a contiguous migration chain; (6) post-migration normalization handles carbonate state consistency and stability tracker seeding for saves that predate those fields; (7) the migration contract documentation in MIGRATIONS is detailed enough for later contributors to follow. The `from_value` public API avoids redundant serialization round-trips for the HTTP handler path. The invariants module correctly separates validation (check-only) from enforcement (check + clamp). One minor UX asymmetry found in error messaging."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"d40ee2b3-877d-4965-b213-497c204c3b3c"}
